# Ubuntu 20.04 (focal) is EOL - fixes for the following CVEs are not backported.
# This is a short-lived CI action (runs, posts a comment, exits) with no persistent
# network exposure, so the attack surface for each CVE is negligible.

# linux-libc-dev - kernel header files required at runtime by the Swift compiler.
# danger-swift compiles Dangerfile.swift on every run, so linux-libc-dev cannot be removed.
# NOTE: These CVEs are in the Linux kernel itself, NOT in the header files provided by
# linux-libc-dev. Container images do not run their own kernel — they share the host kernel.
# Trivy flags linux-libc-dev because it maps kernel CVEs to the user-space headers package,
# but the headers are static files that cannot be exploited through container workloads.
# Exploitation would require a vulnerable host kernel, which is outside the scope of this image.
CVE-2023-52664
CVE-2023-52927
